cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or its results in published work, please cite the
  relevant version below AND the underlying physics references listed at
  the bottom. See docs/DATA_SOURCES.md for the full list of observational
  data sources used and how to cite them. v0.4-prelim+T88E (Tier-1
  milestone 2026-09-04: T72 DAMPE POC, T73 DAMPE CRE forward-model +
  joint-fit integration as Channel 17, T74 Zhang+2025 LSS / assembly-bias
  as Channel 18, T75 v0.7 full T41 rerun at nlive=500, T76 nlive=2000
  convergence check + doc-prominence fix; v0.7 result: log Z = -163.29
  +/- 0.085 (nlive=2000), tension T39 vs Yukawa a = 0.60 (below 1.0
  threshold), MAP m_chi = 770 GeV, sigma/m_0 = 0.27 cm^2/g; T77-T79 LZ
  defensive docs; T80 LZ preprint compatibility; T81 XENONnT/PandaX-4T
  watch as Channel 19; T82 stale-claim audit + CI-gatable drift-guard
  (scripts/t82_audit.py, 44/44 ALL CLEAR); T83 KSFR (3,2) fundamental
  LATTICE promotion; T84 Channel 18 rho sensitivity sweep; T86.7j+k
  plausibility audit + composite-channel gap; T87 composite-DM
  direct-detection forward prediction (verdict: cannot claim LZ event
  at v0.7 MAP, 71 orders below LZ sensitivity); T88.A XRISM Perseus ICM
  Channel 20 silent cross-check; T88.B eROSITA eRASS1 Channel 21
  velocity-gap filler; T88.D XRISM phi->gamgam Channel 22 documented
  null; T88.C Euclid Q1 strong-lensing Channel 23 silent cross-check
  (14 grade-A clusters, Bergamini+ 2026); T88.E Euclid Q1 subhalo dN/dM
  FORECAST Channel 24 - FIRST NON-SILENT channel of T88 series,
  forecast via LensPop pipeline (Collett 2015), expected with Euclid
  DR1 end of 2026; T88 sampling-variance control test (skill P17) ran
  clean: pure T88.E contribution = -0.849 +/- 0.084 (10x noise floor);
  v0.8 result: log Z = -164.87 +/- 0.084 (nlive=2000), MAP m_chi = 770
  GeV, sigma/m_0 = 0.06 cm^2/g, MAP a = 0.13 (was 0.34 at v0.7); T88.E
  pulls posterior 5x lower in sigma/m_0 + 2.6x lower in a (steep
  velocity slope keeps sigma/m(v=150) in the in-band subhalo-survival
  region); T89 Goldstein & Hill 2026 DeltaN_eff<0.107 Channel 25
  documented null (Phys. Rev. D 114, L021305, 2026-07-17; eps^2-
  suppressed at v0.8 MAP, trivially satisfied); T89 sidmkit (Dhiman
  2026, arXiv:2601.04735) + sidm-vdsigmas (Ryan) third-party sigma/m
  benchmark (project T40 Yukawa vs sidmkit Born differ by ~2x at
  galactic velocities - known convention diff, not regression);
  T89 4 citation corrections (Zhang+ 2025 GD-1 anchor, Adhikari+ 2025
  RMP canonical reference, Nadler+ 2025 SIDM Concerto, Jia+ 2026
  Jeans); 677 tests passing; 22 effective channels; drift-guard
  44/44 ALL CLEAR. Standing posture: LZ used as Channel 5 sanity check,
  NOT as sigma/m constraint.
  Earlier closed rounds: T71.4 (3 v0.6 items in parallel: hier-sparc
  +0.10 log Z, bullet_sens +1.74 log Z, CHANNEL_STATUS dict); T71.3
  (R7 closure: nlive=2000 (Nc,Nf) scan via 7-way parallel background
  runner, scan converged); T71.2 (R16 closure: ksfr_mask_max_at_runtime
  field + config_hash field, 575/0/6 tests); T71.1 (R15 closure:
  inelastic + nlive=2000 + KSFR mask extension confound found). The KIV
  cron 080d2f590251 (registered 2026-09-02) re-checks the LZ paper on
  2026-11-01 (60 days after the LZ announcement).
